    "decision_summary": "No public GB API provides <= 1 s frequency data with same-day latency (NESO 1 s has a 5-45 day monthly publication lag, with Sep 2026 as the latest file on 8 Nov 2026). Elexon BMRS (/bmrs/api/v1/system/frequency/stream) provides true UTC 15 s instantaneous samples with 32-142 s live latency (~0.5-2.4 min). At native 15 s timestamps, Elexon matches NESO with lag = 0 s (RMSE = 0.68-1.04 mHz, 88.5-89.4% exact match through 2026-01-11; RMSE = 5.55-7.97 mHz from 2026-02-13 onward due to 3.5-6.3 mHz extra independent-transducer scatter). In 24 h localization trials (n = 400, sigma = 2 mHz), linearly interpolating Real Elexon 15 s to 1 s achieves P(top-1 within +-15 s) = 0.180 (2 min), 0.805 (5 min), 0.985 (10 min), and 0.998 (20 min), outperforming 15 s point matching (0.125, 0.733, 0.965, 0.995)."
  },
